      "source": [
        "# Classification Track (Part A) — Adult Census Income Prediction\n",
        "### 23CSE301 Machine Learning Capstone — Review 1\n",
        "\n",
        "**Dataset:** UCI Adult / Census Income dataset (`adult.data` + `adult.test` merged) — 48,842 records of U.S. census respondents.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** Predict whether a person's annual income exceeds $50K (`income`: `<=50K` / `>50K`) from demographic and employment features.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Scope note:** Per the course guidelines, Classification Part A (Review 1) covers the first 5 algorithms — Logistic Regression, KNN,\n",
        "Naive Bayes, Decision Tree, and SVM. Part B (Random Forest, AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, Bagging, MLP) and the consolidated 10-algorithm\n",
        "table are Review 2 scope and are not included here.\n",
        "\n",
        "All random operations use `random_state=42` for reproducibility."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "id": "b0591b47",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, cross_val_score, StratifiedKFold, GridSearchCV\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\n",
        "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
        "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\n",
        "from sklearn.naive_bayes import GaussianNB\n",
        "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, plot_tree\n",
        "from sklearn.svm import SVC\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, f1_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n",
        "                              roc_auc_score, confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay, roc_curve)\n",
        "\n",
        "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n",
        "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid', palette='colorblind')\n",
        "plt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 100"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "09f66fdb",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Section A — Dataset Loading & Exploratory Data Analysis"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b0b94e41",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### A1. Dataset Loading & Audit"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "faedcafc",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Note on missing values:** the raw UCI Adult files mark missing entries with the literal string `?` rather than leaving the\n",
        "field blank. `na_values=['?']` tells `pandas` to parse those cells as genuine `NaN` on load, so `.isna().sum()` below correctly reports\n",
        "them as missing instead of silently treating `\"?\"` as a valid category value."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "id": "88026943",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv('../data/adult.csv', na_values=['?'])\n",
        "print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)\n",
        "df.head()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "id": "cb53c9a5",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Data types:\\n\")\n",
        "print(df.dtypes)\n",
        "print(\"\\nMissing values per column:\\n\")\n",
        "print(df.isna().sum())\n",
        "print(\"\\nDuplicate rows:\", df.duplicated().sum())"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "id": "d8957e67",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Target ('income') class distribution:\\n\")\n",
        "print(df['income'].value_counts())\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(df['income'].value_counts(normalize=True).round(4))"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "99bb3f7d",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Observation:** 48,842 rows, 15 columns. Three categorical columns (`workclass`, `occupation`, `native-country`) contain missing\n",
        "values (originally encoded as `?` in the raw files) — around 5–6% of rows are affected. There are 52 exact duplicate rows. The target is\n",
        "**imbalanced**: ~76% earn `<=50K` vs. ~24% earn `>50K`, which is why we use a **stratified** train/test split and report **weighted** F1/\n",
        "Precision/Recall (accuracy alone would be misleading on an imbalanced target)."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "661d73bf",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### A2. EDA Visualisations"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "id": "d16bdcff",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "sns.countplot(data=df, x='income', hue='income', palette='colorblind', legend=False)\n",
        "plt.title('Target Distribution — Income Class')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Income'); plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.savefig('clf_target_distribution.png', bbox_inches='tight')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    }
  ]
